# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Generated site data — every build writes here (slates, fantasy, NBA,
# Polymarket, UFC) and `ledger.export_json` writes record.json, which is
# the operator's own betting journal and bankroll. All of it regenerates
# from the build scripts, none of it belongs on the remote. Ignoring the
# directory (not a file list) so a NEW build target can't silently start
# tracking output again.
web/data/

# Downloaded / cached data feeds
data/cache/

# Trained models (regenerate with: python3 train_model.py)
data/models/

# Local API keys — never commit these
secrets.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Historical database (populate with: python3 ingest.py)
data/history.db
*.db
data/ledger.db
data/backups/
# Both forms on purpose. A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, and a
# symlink is not a directory to git — so `node_modules/` alone let a symlink
# named node_modules be committed, pointing at a scratchpad path that exists
# on no other machine. That broke `git pull` for everyone else with
# "Updating the following directories would lose untracked files".
node_modules
node_modules/
